.ft B
MathDB 352972: The Flat Balance Conjecture
Refuted through Generic Finite-Graph Bridges
.ft P
.ps 10.5
.vs 13.5
.sp 1
.ce 1
Formal certificate, lane flat-balance-bridges-formal-pi-r5 (single agent, no children)
.sp 0.5
.ce 1
Lean v4.34.1 (5045d0056413266e57c625dcd7c365b10e377c52); mathlib d13f23b723b8a846827a245b89c10fc7d3f11612
.sp 1
.ft P
This note documents the completed formal certificate for MathDB item 352972,
the flat balance conjecture for finite simple graphs. The refutation is
re-derived from a fully generic bridge layer over arbitrary finite simple
graphs: the c(0) = 1 convention, finite support and cutoff invariance of the
parity clique sums, an exact convention decomposition, integer and real cast
bridges for the discrepancy, and a generic contrapositive. All results are
machine-checked under warnings-as-errors with a strict kernel recheck and a
fresh source-only cleanroom replay. The environment audit enumerates 156
declarations with axiom closure exactly {propext, Classical.choice,
Quot.sound}. The controls record contains ten positive proofs.
.sp 1
.ft B
1. Scope and corrected metadata (M1)
.ft P
.ti 3n
This certificate revises and completes the earlier author draft. Two
metadata corrections are recorded here and in results/352972.json. First,
the controls file audit/Controls352972Bridges.lean contains TEN positive
proof examples, every one a compiling proof; no failed compilation is
counted as a control. Second, the contrapositive control (C9) is proved from
the discrepancy hypothesis alone: it consumes no flatness hypothesis, and no
use of Flat is claimed for it. The earlier author files are preserved
untouched.
.sp 0.8
.ft B
2. Source-level statements
.ft P
.ti 3n
The source layer (module FlatBalance, 502 lines) defines finite simple graphs
as a structure with symmetry and irreflexivity proofs, clique sets as
edge-complete Finsets of vertices, the clique counts c(k), the parity weighted
sums oddCliqueSum and evenCliqueSum over range (card V + 1), the flatness
predicate Flat, balancedness Balanced as discrepancyNat at most one, and the
conjecture FlatBalancedConjecture. The K(3,3) witness on Fin 3 (+) Fin 3 is
exhibited flat with clique counts c(0) = 1, c(1) = 6, c(2) = 9, giving odd
sum 7 and even sum 10, discrepancy 3 under the positive-index convention and
4 under the c(0)-inclusive convention; either exceeds one. The literal
endpoint not_flat_balanced_conjecture is the source refutation.
.bp
.ft B
3. The generic bridge layer (R1)
.ft P
.ti 3n
The new module FlatBalanceBridges proves everything below over an arbitrary
finite simple graph G on any vertex type V; the witness is used only at the
final instantiation.
.sp 0.5
.ft B
3.1 The c(0) = 1 convention, empty graphs included
.ft P
.ti 3n
Theorem cliqueFinset_zero: for every G, the 0-cliques are exactly the
singleton of the empty vertex set. Theorem cliqueCount_zero: c(G,0) = 1.
Both are unconditional in G, so they apply to the empty graph and to every
discrete graph; the convention is a theorem, not an assumption.
.sp 0.5
.ft B
3.2 Finite support and cutoff invariance
.ft P
.ti 3n
Lemma cliqueFinset_empty_of_card_lt and cliqueCount_of_card_lt: no k-cliques
exist once card V < k, since every vertex Finset embeds in univ. The private
range-extension lemma sum_range_cutoff states that a finitely supported
summand has cutoff-independent partial sums. Consequently, for any cutoff N
with card V < N, the odd selector sum over range N equals oddCliqueSum G
(oddCliqueSum_cutoff), and likewise for the even selector with c(0) included
(evenCliqueSum_cutoff) and the positive-index even part
(evenCliqueSumPos_cutoff). The parity sums therefore have honest finite
support; no hidden divergence or convention-dependent truncation exists.
.sp 0.5
.ft B
3.3 Convention separation by an exact decomposition
.ft P
.ti 3n
Theorem evenCliqueSum_decomp: evenCliqueSum G = c(G,0) + evenCliqueSumPos G,
pointwise in G, via the term split (if d = 0 then c else 0) plus (if d even
and d > 0 then c else 0). The two source conventions remain distinct
objects; neither is substituted for the other anywhere in the certificate.
Theorem oddAddEvenCliqueSum recombines the parity selectors into the plain
clique-count sum.
.sp 0.5
.ft B
3.4 Cast bridges and bound equivalence
.ft P
.ti 3n
natAbs_cast_abs: the integer cast of Int.natAbs z is the true |z| in Z; no
truncated natural subtraction enters any cast. natAbs_cast_real lifts this
to R for natural inputs, and discrepancyNat_cast_real transports the
discrepancy exactly: the real cast of discrepancyNat G equals the absolute
value of the difference of the real casts of the odd and even clique sums.
balanced_iff_absInt and balanced_iff_absReal: Balanced G agrees with the
absolute-value bound at most one, over Z and over R respectively. The
endpoint hypothesis therefore transfers through the cast layer without
reproof.
.sp 0.5
.ft B
3.5 The generic contrapositive and the endpoint
.ft P
.ti 3n
not_balanced_of_one_lt_discrepancy: any finite simple graph whose clique
count discrepancy exceeds one is not balanced; the proof uses the
discrepancy hypothesis and nothing else. flat_not_balanced_exists_via_bridges
instantiates the contrapositive at K(3,3) via the source lemma
K33_discrepancy_gt_one, and not_flat_balanced_conjecture_via_bridges
re-derives the literal negated universal. The bridge layer is thus formally
connected to the source-level conjecture negation; no bridge lemma is idle.
.bp
.ft B
4. Machine-checked environment audit (R2)
.ft P
.ti 3n
audit/FlatBalanceEnvAudit.lean walks the elaborated environment of both
production modules and enumerates every declaration, generated and private
ones included: 156 declarations. Kind, definition safety, origin module, full
type, full value body when present, and the complete transitive axiom closure
are printed for each. The scan reports zero unsafe, zero partial and zero
opaque declarations. The union of axioms over all 156 declarations is exactly
{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}. The transitive constant closure of
each endpoint refutation contains 14 local constants and the axioms
{Classical.choice, Quot.sound}; propext enters only through the Finset
extensionality used in the bridge layer itself.
.sp 0.8
.ft B
5. Positive proof controls (M1)
.ft P
.ti 3n
audit/Controls352972Bridges.lean, receipt 1794089496104554182, contains ten
positive proofs. C1, C2: the generic empty-clique shape and c(G,0) = 1 for
every finite simple graph, empty graphs included; plus the witness instance
c(K33,0) = 1 and a zero-vertex instance. C4: generic finite support, no
7-cliques on six vertices. C5, C6: cutoff invariance instances for the odd
and even selectors. C7: the exact convention decomposition instance. C8: the
integer natAbs cast bridge. C9: the generic contrapositive instance; by the
metadata correction its proof uses only the discrepancy hypothesis. C10: the
real bound-equivalence instance for the witness.
.sp 0.8
.ft B
6. Cleanroom replay (R3)
.ft P
.ti 3n
The cleanroom under cleanroom/ starts from an empty build directory and holds
source-only copies of the two production modules; their sha256 digests equal
the lane sources (source-hashmap.json). The replay compiles both modules with
-DwarningAsError=true -M3500 -j1 under a two-CPU affinity and an isolated
LEAN_PATH containing only the fresh build directory and the pinned upstream
libraries; the earlier lane build output appears in no path used by the
replay. leanchecker re-verifies both oleans at the kernel level.
EXTRACTION-RECEIPT.json records the tool version, dependency revisions,
flags, and all hashes. The lane build directory carries no legacy path in the
final state.
.sp 0.8
.ft B
7. Recorded failed attempts
.ft P
.ti 3n
Failed attempts are recorded with their receipts, not silently discarded: the
first cast section draft (implicit NatCast and Real elaboration) failed on
instance synthesis; a placeholder argument in the h4 cast step and a misplaced
Real import failed next; the first controls draft left one goal open; the
first environment audit draft used a nonexistent DefinitionSafety constructor
and a brace-escaping form. Each has a receipt in receipt/ and a log in logs/,
and each was fixed in place; no fabricated failure is claimed anywhere.
.sp 0.8
.ft B
8. Artifacts
.ft P
.ti 3n
results/352972.json (final record); MANIFEST-352972-final.json (sha256
manifest over sources, receipts, logs and cleanroom outputs, with named
non-circular exclusions); EXTRACTION-RECEIPT.json; source-hashmap.json; audit
and controls receipts. Independent audit and root acceptance remain outside
this lane and are not self-credited.
